course: dictionary
lesson: 3888
title: One word, two jobs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words can do more than one job. Frequent can describe a thing, or it can be a verb that tells you what someone does. Look at where the word sits in the sentence to find its job.
explain: As an adjective, frequent describes a noun: «Ireland's frequent rain keeps the grass green all year.» Here frequent means happening often. Ask yourself: is the word describing something, or is someone doing something?
explain: As a verb, frequent means to go to a place often. The clue is a place after the word and a sense of repeating: «The fishermen frequented the harbour every morning.» Swap in «went to often» and it still makes sense. Test any meaning by putting it into the sentence.
fact: Frequent means happening often.
fact: To frequent a place means to go there often (formal). The verb is said free-KWENT.
fact: In maths, frequency means how often something happens, for example in a tally chart.
fact: The mode is the most frequent value, the one that appears most often in a set of data.
fact: «Frequent visitor», «frequent flyer» and «frequent breaks» all mean something happens or comes often.
exercise: «Frequent nosebleeds in children are rarely serious.» What does frequent mean here? | Very large | Bright red | Sudden and scary | *Happening often
exercise: In a maths lesson, the mode is the most frequent value. What does most frequent mean? | Smallest number | Happens least often | Biggest number | *Happens most often
exercise: Aunt Mae says, «I frequent the library on Fridays.» What does frequent mean? | Close down | Read very quickly | *Go to often | Stay away from
test: «Frequent breaks help you stay fresh during a long day.» Which phrase is the best swap for frequent? | Loud | Long | Rare | *Often
test: A fan says, «I frequent the stadium.» What does frequent mean here? | Forgets | Builds | Dislikes | *Goes to often
exam: Which sentence uses frequent as an adjective, describing a noun? | We frequented the park | *Frequent rain keeps the grass green all year | They frequent the harbour each day | She will frequent the library soon
